====== Vizio XWR100 ====== 

Cheap router with dualband.

===== Supported Versions =====

Supported with souce code hosted on github: [[https://github.com/cmtsij/openwrt_XWR100/]]


===== Hardware Highlights =====
^ SoC                       ^ Ram    ^ Flash   ^ Network   ^ USB   ^ Serial   ^ JTag   ^
| Atheros AR7161 @ 680MHz   | 32MB   | 8MB     | 4 x 1     | Yes   | Yes      | No     |


===== Hardware =====
==== Info ====

^ Architecture         | MIPS                                                      |
^ Vendor               | VIZIO                                                     |
^ Bootloader           | U-Boot                                                    |
^ System-On-Chip       | Atheros AR7161                                            |
^ CPU Speed            | 680 MHz                                                   |
^ Flash-Chip           | STMicroelectronics M25P64-VMF6P                           |
^ Flash size           | 8 MiB                                                     |
^ RAM                  | 32 MiB                                                    |
^ Wireless             | Two radio chips: 2.4GHz 802.11B/G/N and 5GHz 802.11A/N.   |
^ 2.4GHz 802.11B/G/N   | AR9227                                                    |
^ 5GHz 802.11A/N       | AR9220                                                    |
^ Ethernet             | AR8216: 4x 10/100 Mbps LAN, 1x 10/100 Mbps WAN            |
^ USB                  | Yes                                                       |
^ Serial               | [[#Serial|Yes]]                                           |
^ JTAG                 | no                                                        |

==== Serial ====
There is a serial header mounted on the board with the following pinout: 

^         JP1              ^^^^
|   1   |  2   |  3   |   4   |
|  Vcc  |  Tx  |   Rx | GND   |


